Owner directive: 'Nothing should be blocking. Nothing stale should just sit there blocking.'

Three rules in the hot lane (the six deep-tape slots that carry a coin's live order book to the Judge)
held a slot against a coin that had stopped earning it, or refused a coin for ever on one look:

1. A hot pair was evicted ONLY to make room for a new nominee. With nothing new arriving, a coin whose
   run ended an hour ago kept its subscription — and its share of a main thread at 88-91% — for ever.
   Now: a slot is held only while the coin is still nominated (the watch's band of 12 is the
   hysteresis); the moment it is not, it yields, waiting nominee or not. That path needs no venue
   verification, so it runs before the selectUniverse guard.
2. tenureMs was a two-hour FLOOR: even with a fresh runner waiting, the stale pair kept the slot.
   Now minHoldMs = 10 min — a thrash guard, not a lease.
3. NOT_VERIFIED_BY_VENUE_SELECTION was remembered in 'seen', so a coin the venue check refused once was
   never looked at again that session. A runner's 24h volume BUILDS WHILE IT RUNS: under the floor at
   03:00 and well over it at 10:00 is the normal shape of the thing we hunt. That refusal is now
   retryable and never remembered.

Held/pending exposure is never released. The Judge's law is untouched; authority NONE throughout.

tape/run.js re-pinned (4ae7c8a9 -> 4e35ceac) with its audit entry in the SCOPE-5 fence.

Tests: publish-fix-96-nothing-stale-blocks 5/5 — all five fail on the previous code. tape-hot-lane 4/4
updated to the new law. Green: social-4f-scope 9, universe 9, wideeye 6, publish-fix-94 7,
learning-volatility-watch 4, tape-resource-law 3, judge-composition 4, paper-runtime 8, coin-dossier 3.

